  "query_preview": "..\nDistant Tropical Storm Dujuan has moved north of 25N and has exited\nthe region. Dujuan continues to steer relatively drier air south of \n20N, leading to spotty showers across Tinian and Saipan, then showers\nbecome increasingly scattered across Guam and Rota, closer in \nproximity to the trailing band of monsoonal moisture and convergence.\nScattered showers and isolated thunderstorms prevail across the \nregion, moreso across Guam and Rota through Saturday, then showers \nspread northward across Tinian and Saipan early next week. A brief \nperiod of numerous showers are expected to build across southern Guam\nwaters overnight, with locally heavy showers and occasional gusts to\n25 mph possible across Guam. The main band of monsoonal moisture \ncontinues to linger near and south of Guam, with model guidance \nshowing some potential of a nearby weak disturbance forming in the \nmonsoon trough early next week. Depending on this scenario or if \nthere is a northward shift in the monsoon trough, this could \npotentially result in periods of scattered to numerous showers with \nmoderate to strong gusts early next week.",
